  "predicted_delta_text": "**Prediction**: NF_db improves by ~0.4 dB.  \n*Rationale*: The failure is dominated by excessive noise figure due to high input-referred noise from the NMOS input transistor (NM1) and poor noise matching. The current gate biasing of NM1 via R1\u2013R2 is unstable and results in suboptimal transconductance and noise performance. Adding NM3 (diode-connected NMOS) between n6 and n3 creates a current mirror-like feedback path that stabilizes the gate voltage of NM1, reducing noise by improving bias point stability and increasing effective transconductance. This is a classic technique for improving noise performance in LNA topologies.\n\n---",
